The owner's agent workflow, a separate tool shared by several projects, was
wired to beads (bd): its skills, its commands and its config named bd
directly. Once the format and script were stable, map the concepts across,
migrate any existing bd data, and update what names bd.

What it turned out to be (2026-09-18 to 2026-09-21). The wiring was not this
project's: it lived in the workflow tool's own repository and its global
install, shared by every project on the machine, three of which were actively
on beads. Rewriting it to say pidly would have switched those projects onto a
tracker they had not imported. The owner chose to make the workflow
tracker-agnostic instead: a project names its tracker in config, and an
absent setting means beads, so nothing that works today breaks.

That was a change to the other tool rather than to pidly, and it landed
there: a Tracker interface, implemented for beads and for pidly, the latter
reading tickets as files rather than shelling out (a 445-ticket tracker
answers in 0.58s), with only mutations going through the script for the lock.
This repository's own half was three config lines, done once that landed.

Two things do not map, and are refused rather than faked:

  assignee   a claim names a process that can be verified; writing a person
             into it would invent the unverifiable claim this format refuses
  labels     no home here, so routing by domain label does not reach a pidly
             project unless it declares a labels field of its own (see 35)

Priority and kind do map, because migrate writes fields of those names when
importing from beads.

A migration was trialled against a downstream project's beads tracker as a
dry run into a scratch tracker: 445 issues in, 445 out, pidly check clean,
needs renumbered, beads ids kept so old commit messages still resolve, and
hierarchy kept to depth 6. It turned up 55 (the staleness guard's remedy
could not clear the guard), and an export seven weeks behind its tracker,
which is exactly what migrate's guard exists to refuse.

Not migrated: the other projects stay on beads, which costs them nothing.
The import is proven and can happen whenever each owner wants it.
